### Patch to Fix the Problem

To address the highlighting issue, we need to adjust the regex by ensuring that `infer` and `type` are only considered keywords when they are standalone and not part of a longer identifier.

```javascript
### components/prism-typescript.js
<<<<<<< SEARCH
		/\b(?:asserts|infer|interface|module|namespace|type)(?!\s*[^\s_${}*a-zA-Z\xA0-\uFFFF])/
=======
		/\b(?:asserts|infer|interface|module|namespace|type)\b(?!\s*[^\s_${}*a-zA-Z\xA0-\uFFFF])/
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

This patch adds a `\b` word boundary after the keyword to ensure it is identified only when it occurs as a standalone word.
